From 8cd673eb611dcc99097b43ef404ade2bddd06819 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Andrew Youll <andrewyoull86@gmail.com>
Date: Mon, 28 Sep 2026 16:48:30 +0100
Subject: [PATCH 18/18] avformat: TLS through RISC OS's AcornSSL module (https)

--enable-riscos-acornssl: the tls protocol (and so https, tls, rtmps and
HLS over https) through the AcornSSL module of RISC OS 5.28 and later.
The TCP connection is opened as usual; its RISC OS socket is handed to
AcornSSL_CreateSession, and reading and writing go through AcornSSL_Recv
and AcornSSL_Send (non-blocking, waiting on the socket with the timeout
and interrupt callback). The handshake is driven with 1-byte peeks until
AcornSSL stops returning ENOTCONN; the host name is set for SNI and the
certificate check. Certificates are always checked by AcornSSL, which asks
the desktop user about one it can't verify.
---
 configure                  |   7 +-
 libavformat/Makefile       |   1 +
 libavformat/tls_acornssl.c | 340 +++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++
 3 files changed, 347 insertions(+), 1 deletion(-)
 create mode 100644 libavformat/tls_acornssl.c

